  "result": {
    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.delete_edge - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.delete_edge.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.delete_edge()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Delete an edge from the graph.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.delete_edge()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Delete an edge from the graph.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.delete_edge()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Delete an edge from the graph.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nDelete an edge from the graph.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L3025-L3183){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.delete_edge(\n    source=None,\n    target=None,\n    id=None,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Delete edge](../assets/graphs/delete-edge.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Before: a four-node cycle with the edge between A and C highlighted in the accent color. After: that edge is gone, shown dashed, while all four nodes and the other three edges stay in place.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nRemove edges by specifying either the source and target nodes, or the edge ID directly. For\nmultigraphs with source/target, only the first matching edge is deleted.\n\nOnly the edge is removed; both endpoint nodes stay in the graph, even if they end up\nisolated. When deleting by endpoints, direction matters in a directed graph (deleting\n`B -> A` won't remove an `A -> B` edge), while in an undirected graph the endpoints can be\ngiven in either order. When several parallel edges connect the pair, call the method\nrepeatedly, or use `delete_edge_by_id()` to pick a specific one. The graph is modified in\nplace and the deletion is recorded in the step log (see `steps`).\n\nTo remove many edges matching a condition, select them and use `delete_edges_ws()`.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[source]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Union[int, str, None]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Source node ID or label. Required (together with `target=`) if `id=` is not provided.\n    In a directed graph this must be the node the edge starts from.\n\n<code>[target]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Union[int, str, None]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Target node ID or label. Required (together with `source=`) if `id=` is not provided.\n\n<code>[id]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Edge ID to delete. If provided, `source=` and `target=` are ignored. Edge IDs can be\n    found with `get_edge_ids()`, `find_edge_ids()` or the `id` column of the edge\n    DataFrame. Default is `None`.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Self for method chaining.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [EdgeNotFoundError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If no edge exists matching the criteria (no edge between the two nodes, or no edge\n    with the given ID). It is a subclass of both `KeyError` and `ValueError`.\n\n<code> [NodeNotFoundError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `source=` or `target=` doesn't match any node (also a `KeyError` and a\n    `ValueError`).\n\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If neither (`source`, `target`) nor `id` is provided.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~delete_edge_by_id`) \n\n:   Remove one edge by its ID.\n\n[](`~delete_edges_ws`) \n\n:   Delete the selected edges.\n\n[](`~delete_node`) \n\n:   Remove a node and its edges.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nProviding both `source` and `target` deletes the first matching edge between them. The\nnodes themselves are kept:\n\n::: {#f3272ab1 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges([(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\")], directed=True)\ngraph.delete_edge(source=\"A\", target=\"B\")\n\ngraph.has_edge(source=\"A\", target=\"B\"), graph.count_nodes()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n(False, 3)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nIn a directed graph the endpoints must be given in the edge's direction. Asking for the\nreverse `C -> B` edge raises a `KeyError`:\n\n::: {#9de6e5d5 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ntry:\n    graph.delete_edge(source=\"C\", target=\"B\")\nexcept KeyError as e:\n    print(e)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n```\nNo edge found from 'C' to 'B'\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nWith parallel edges, each call removes only one of them, so the second edge (weight\n`2.0`) survives:\n\n::: {#25fae67c .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges([(\"A\", \"B\", 1.0), (\"A\", \"B\", 2.0)])\ngraph.delete_edge(source=\"A\", target=\"B\")\n\ngraph.get_edge_df()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div><style>\n.dataframe > thead > tr,\n.dataframe > tbody > tr {\n  text-align: right;\n  white-space: pre-wrap;\n}\n</style>\n<small>shape: (1, 5)</small><table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\"><thead><tr><th>id</th><th>source</th><th>target</th><th>rel</th><th>weight</th></tr><tr><td>i64</td><td>i64</td><td>i64</td><td>null</td><td>f64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>2</td><td>null</td><td>2.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### A payment reversed\n\nIn `payments()`, eight accounts can all reach each other by following payments: the two\ncircles of large payments, Ana, Ben and Cruz, and Finn, Gus and Hal, together with Dee\nand Eve. Strongly connected components find them, and the flatmates Max and Nia, who pay\neach other:\n\n::: {#e83d174a .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\npayments = ec.payments()\n\ncycles = payments.strongly_connected_components()\nsorted(len(c) for c in cycles if len(c) > 1)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```\n[2, 8]\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nEve's payment of 2,000 to Finn was the only way for money to reach Finn's circle. If the\nbank reverses it, Finn, Gus and Hal can still pay the others (Gus pays Dee), but nothing\ncomes back, and the eight split into a group of five and Finn's circle of three:\n\n::: {#200b6ca5 .cell execution_count=5}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\npayments.delete_edge(\"Eve\", \"Finn\")\n\ncycles = payments.strongly_connected_components()\nsorted(len(c) for c in cycles if len(c) > 1)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=5}\n```\n[2, 3, 5]\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#ae414811 .cell execution_count=6}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\npayments.plot(\n    highlight=[\"Finn\", \"Gus\", \"Hal\", \"Finn\"], label_by=\"label\", seed=3\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=6}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</style